    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new collision-resolution logic sits naturally in `generateCustomerCode`, which is the unit already responsible for producing the stored customer code \u2014 the right place for a concern that depends on the service-level `ownerRepository`.\n\nIt also matches the established idiom of this class exactly. Its sibling private helpers `countNamesakes` (line 327) and `countHouseholdMembers` (line 347) use the identical `ownerRepository.findAll().stream().filter(... !Objects.equals(getId(), owner.getId()) ...)` pattern to compare against other owners while excluding self. So the `findAll()`-plus-stream approach (rather than a derived `existsByCustomerCode` query method) is consistent with the surrounding conventions, not a one-off; a maintainer here would find it natural.\n\nNo duplication, the method hasn't become a catch-all, and the null-base early return and the Javadoc update are coherent with the rest of the file.",
